      "writtenOn": "2022-10-05T21:10:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Consider void* fItemArray\nint fCount;\nuint32_t fReserve : 31;\nuint32_t fOwnMemory : 1;\n\nWith this fCount does not need any masking to access, and I think it is accessed more frequently than fReserve.\n\nSo, with the old order when accessing fReserve it will have to be masked with 0x7ffffff, which is a big instruction. Now it is a logical shift right by 1 which is a small instruction.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 37,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 37,
        "endChar": 30
      },
      "revId": "041919784680d0de9b8ecf74b45cd07ee57e3751",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1ec47fcd_a3d4bcd1",
        "filename": "include/private/SkTArray.h",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 37,
      "author": {
        "id": 5641
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-06T14:39:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Both fCount and fAllocCount are accessed frequently, so it would make sense to apply the same treatment.  Maybe adding a separate word for flags is a reasonable trade off?\n\nThe original intent was to split off type-independent code while minimizing the size of the change -- not to rework SkTArray.\n\nThere certainly are refactoring opportunities, but it\u0027s wise to keep those separate.\n\nLet me take another pass, and see which parts make sense and which don\u0027t.",
      "parentUuid": "1ec02027_5468c9ae",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 37,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 37,
        "endChar": 30
      },
      "revId": "041919784680d0de9b8ecf74b45cd07ee57e3751",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
